cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WaveBench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "WaveBench: signal processing in the browser for accelerometer and sensor records"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kilic
    given-names: Kursat
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kilickursat/WaveBench"
url: "https://kilickursat.github.io/WaveBench/"
abstract: >-
  WaveBench is an open-source signal-processing workbench that runs in the web browser. It imports raw sensor records
  such as 3-axis accelerometer logs, checks or assigns their timebase, applies Butterworth and notch filters, and
  computes FFT spectra, Welch power spectral densities and STFT spectrograms. Analyses run in Float64 on the CPU,
  validated against SciPy and 50-digit references, or in Float32 with WebGPU compute shaders validated against the
  Float64 engine.
keywords:
  - signal processing
  - FFT
  - STFT
  - spectrogram
  - power spectral density
  - Welch method
  - Butterworth filter
  - accelerometer
  - vibration analysis
  - WebGPU
